# ========== Documentation Files (root level only) ==========
# Deny-by-default: internal planning docs, audits and scratch notes at the repo
# root stay out of git, so they cannot leak into the public repository. The
# files meant for the outside world are allowed back in one by one below — add
# to that list rather than relaxing the rule, and check `git check-ignore -v`
# on any new root-level doc before assuming it was committed.
/*.md
!README.md
!API.md
!SECURITY.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!CHANGELOG.md

# Internal planning spreadsheets (the launch tracker and anything like it).
# Same deny-by-default reasoning as the markdown rule above: these carry
# internal status, owners and known-weakness notes and must never ship.
/*.xlsx
/*.xlsm

# Specifically ignore these documentation files
/ALL_PROJECTS_IMPLEMENTATION.md
/BACKEND_ANALYSIS_SUMMARY.md
/BACKEND_API_ENDPOINTS_SUMMARY.md
/BACKEND_API_GAPS.md
/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE_ANALYSIS.md
/DASHBOARD_IMPLEMENTATION.md
/DESIGN_SYSTEM.json
/INTEGRATION_PLAN.md
/LOGIN_PAGE_IMPLEMENTATION.md
/PAGES_INVENTORY.md
/PAGES_LIST.md
/PHASE_1_COMPLETE.md
/PROJECT_ANALYSIS_SUMMARY.md
/QUICK_START_GUIDE.md
/README_BACKEND_ANALYSIS.md
/UI_REPLACEMENT_SUMMARY.md

